  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::MunicipalRecord
  interactionName: Resident
  isInformationSource: 1
  npcProfile: 0
  openingLine: It's been a quiet day around here.
  choice1: Ask about Daniel
  response1: Daniel Mercer disappeared seven years ago.
  choice2: Ask about the town
  response2: Nothing much changes around here.
  informationID: municipal_waterworks_archived_floor_plan
  informationTitle: Archived Waterworks Floor Plan
  informationSource: Grayford Municipal Records
  informationDescription: An archived North County Waterworks floor plan, revised in 1987, depicts the lower service corridor and an adjoining inspection chamber accessed through the original service doorway. The chamber is identified as part of the facility's drainage inspection infrastructure. The plan predates the alterations recorded in 1991 and does not establish the chamber's later condition or use.
  informationType: 2
  isSceneExit: 0
  destinationScene: Diner_Investigation
  destinationSpawnID: 
  requiredInformationID: waterworks_original_access_mechanism
  unavailableMessage: The archive holds many historical plans. I need a clearer reason to look for the original lower-access layout.
  department: "Grayford Public Works \u2014 Engineering Archives"
  documentTitle: Waterworks Floor Plan
  reference: NCW-PL-87-04 / Sheet L2
  documentDate: June 16, 1987
  documentBody: "NORTH COUNTY WATERWORKS\r\n\r\nLOWER SERVICE LEVEL \u2014 GENERAL ARRANGEMENT\r\n\r\nIDENTIFIED AREAS\r\n\r\nL-01 \u2014 Lower Service Corridor\r\n\r\nL-02 \u2014 Drainage Inspection Chamber\r\n\r\nL-03 \u2014 Auxiliary Pump Access\r\n\r\nL-04 \u2014 Pipe Maintenance Recess\r\n\r\nACCESS ARRANGEMENT\r\n\r\nThe drainage inspection chamber (L-02) is accessed from the lower service corridor (L-01) through a hinged service doorway.\r\n\r\nThe doorway is shown as part of the original facility arrangement. No secondary barrier is indicated on this revision.\r\n\r\nARCHIVE NOTE\r\n\r\nThis drawing represents the facility arrangement as recorded in June 1987. Subsequent modifications may not be reflected.\r\n\r\nLater revisions should be consulted before relying on this plan for current access or safety information."
  evidenceID: municipal_waterworks_archived_floor_plan
  evidenceTitle: Archived Waterworks Floor Plan
  journalNote: A 1987 plan shows Chamber L-02 reached through a hinged door from corridor L-01, with no additional barrier shown.
  evidenceSource: Grayford Municipal Records Office
