MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 276328552}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: ab16c4c9be9f4134e9e1280441fa2bbc, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::MunicipalRecord
  interactionName: Resident
  isInformationSource: 1
  npcProfile: 0
  openingLine: It's been a quiet day around here.
  choice1: Ask about Daniel
  response1: Daniel Mercer disappeared seven years ago.
  choice2: Ask about the town
  response2: Nothing much changes around here.
  informationID: daniel_remains_identification_report
  informationTitle: Identification of Daniel Mercer's Remains
  informationSource: County Medical Examiner's Office
  informationDescription: A supplemental forensic identification report confirms that the human remains recovered from Chamber L-02 belong to Daniel Mercer. Identification was established through comparison with historical dental records. The cause and manner of death remain undetermined.
  informationType: 2
  isSceneExit: 0
  destinationScene: Diner_Investigation
  destinationSpawnID: 
  requiredInformationID: waterworks_preliminary_examination_report
  unavailableMessage: The identification findings are not available in the records I have seen.
  department: County Medical Examiner's Office
  documentTitle: "Supplemental Identification Report \u2014 Waterworks Remains"
  reference: CME-98-104-S1
  documentDate: October 1998
  documentBody: 'Recovery Location:

    North County Waterworks

    Lower Inspection Chamber L-02



    Subject:

    Previously unidentified human skeletal remains



    IDENTIFICATION FINDINGS



    Historical dental records obtained for

    Daniel Mercer were compared with the

    dental structures preserved in the

    recovered remains.



    Multiple corresponding dental features

    were identified, including the position

    and configuration of previous restorations.



    No unexplained discrepancies were observed.



    CONCLUSION



    The recovered remains are identified

    as those of Daniel Mercer.



    CAUSE OF DEATH:

    Undetermined.



    MANNER OF DEATH:

    Undetermined.



    The identification findings do not,

    by themselves, establish the circumstances

    of death or the date on which the remains

    were deposited in the chamber.



    Further investigative correlation is

    recommended.'
  evidenceID: daniel_remains_identification_report
  evidenceTitle: Daniel Mercer's Remains Identified
  journalNote: Dental records identify the remains in Chamber L-02 as Daniel Mercer. His cause and manner of death remain undetermined.
  evidenceSource: County Medical Examiner's Office
