  informationID: municipal_retention_index
  informationTitle: Anonymous package
  informationSource: Anonymous package
  informationDescription: An anonymous sender sent me two waterworks records and a note claiming the original search missed something.
  informationType: 2
  isSceneExit: 0
  destinationScene: Diner_Investigation
  destinationSpawnID: 
  requiredInformationID: municipal_status_ledger
  unavailableMessage: The retention index covers several record types. I need to narrow down which contractor file to trace.
  department: GRAYFORD MUNICIPAL RECORDS
  documentTitle: Records Retention Index
  reference: PW-CONTRACT/1991
  documentDate: 1991
  documentBody: "GRAYFORD MUNICIPAL RECORDS\r\nPUBLIC WORKS \u2014 RECORDS RETENTION INDEX\r\n\r\nRecord Category: Contractor Work Documentation\r\nPeriod: January\u2013December 1991\r\n\r\nMunicipal maintenance registers and work-order status ledgers are retained by the Public Works Department.\r\n\r\nContractor completion reports, site inspection notes, and supporting work documentation are maintained in separate contractor files.\r\n\r\nAssociated Contractor: Bell Municipal Services\r\nReferenced Work Order: WW-91-184\r\n\r\nThe index does not confirm whether a completion report was submitted for this work order."
  evidenceID: municipal_retention_index
  evidenceTitle: Records Retention Index
  journalNote: "Contractor completion reports are indexed separately. The index does not confirm a report for Bell\u2019s WW-91-184."
  evidenceSource: Grayford Municipal Records Office
