  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::MunicipalRecord
  interactionName: Resident
  isInformationSource: 1
  npcProfile: 0
  openingLine: It's been a quiet day around here.
  choice1: Ask about Daniel
  response1: Daniel Mercer disappeared seven years ago.
  choice2: Ask about the town
  response2: Nothing much changes around here.
  informationID: daniel_original_police_report
  informationTitle: Original Missing Person Report
  informationSource: Grayford Sheriff's Department, GF-91-1047
  informationDescription: An archived missing-person report dated October 19, 1991, identifies Deputy Michael Dwyer as the officer responsible for the initial investigation into Daniel Mercer's disappearance. The report records no confirmed movements after October 17 and states that no verified evidence of criminal involvement was established. The case remained unresolved.
  informationType: 2
  isSceneExit: 0
  destinationScene: Diner_Investigation
  destinationSpawnID: 
  requiredInformationID: 
  unavailableMessage: 
  department: Grayford Sheriff's Department
  documentTitle: Missing Person Report
  reference: Case No. GF-91-1047
  documentDate: October 19, 1991
  documentBody: 'Subject: Daniel Mercer

    Last reported seen: October 17, 1991

    Reporting officer: Deputy Michael Dwyer

    Case status: Unresolved



    Summary of initial investigation



    Daniel Mercer was reported missing after failing to return home. Initial inquiries with local residents produced no confirmed account of his whereabouts after October 17.



    No verified evidence of criminal involvement was identified during the preliminary investigation. The subject''s last known movements remain undetermined.



    Disposition



    Case remains open pending additional information.'
  evidenceID: daniel_original_police_report
  evidenceTitle: Original Missing Person Report
  journalNote: "Dwyer handled Daniel\u2019s 1991 disappearance case. Daniel\u2019s movements after October 17 were unverified, and the case remained unresolved."
  evidenceSource: Grayford Sheriff's Office
