  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: ab16c4c9be9f4134e9e1280441fa2bbc, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::MunicipalRecord
  interactionName: Resident
  isInformationSource: 1
  npcProfile: 0
  openingLine: It's been a quiet day around here.
  choice1: Ask about Daniel
  response1: Daniel Mercer disappeared seven years ago.
  choice2: Ask about the town
  response2: Nothing much changes around here.
  informationID: daniel_skeletal_trauma_assessment
  informationTitle: Supplemental Skeletal Trauma Assessment
  informationSource: County Medical Examiner's Office
  informationDescription: A supplemental examination of Daniel Mercer's remains identifies skeletal fractures consistent with substantial blunt-force trauma. A fall from height is among the possible mechanisms, but the examination cannot establish the precise circumstances or determine whether the injuries caused death.
  informationType: 2
  isSceneExit: 0
  destinationScene: Diner_Investigation
  destinationSpawnID: 
  requiredInformationID: daniel_remains_identification_report
  unavailableMessage: "The trauma findings are filed with an identified examination record. I can\u2019t locate the corresponding report yet."
  department: County Medical Examiner's Office
  documentTitle: "Supplemental Skeletal Trauma Assessment \u2014 Daniel Mercer"
  reference: CME-98-104-S2
  documentDate: October 1998
  documentBody: 'Subject: Daniel Mercer

    Recovery Location:

    North County Waterworks, Chamber L-02



    EXAMINATION FINDINGS



    Examination identified fractures involving

    the skeletal structures of the torso

    and upper extremity.



    The observed injury pattern is consistent

    with substantial blunt-force trauma.



    A fall from an elevated position is one

    possible mechanism.



    The skeletal findings do not establish

    the precise mechanism of injury.



    The available evidence is insufficient

    to determine whether the identified

    injuries directly caused death.



    CONCLUSION



    Significant skeletal trauma is present.



    CAUSE OF DEATH:

    Undetermined.



    MANNER OF DEATH:

    Undetermined.



    Correlation with scene findings and

    investigative evidence is recommended.



    End of supplemental assessment.'
  evidenceID: daniel_skeletal_trauma_assessment
  evidenceTitle: Daniel's Skeletal Trauma
  journalNote: "Daniel\u2019s remains show blunt-force fractures consistent with a possible fall. The precise mechanism and cause of death remain undetermined."
  evidenceSource: County Medical Examiner's Office
