  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::MunicipalRecord
  interactionName: Resident
  isInformationSource: 1
  npcProfile: 0
  openingLine: It's been a quiet day around here.
  choice1: Ask about Daniel
  response1: Daniel Mercer disappeared seven years ago.
  choice2: Ask about the town
  response2: Nothing much changes around here.
  informationID: dwyer_equipment_assignment_register
  informationTitle: Sheriff's Equipment Assignment Register
  informationSource: Grayford Sheriff's Department
  informationDescription: An archived October 1991 equipment register lists a portable inspection lamp assigned to Deputy Michael Dwyer. The lamp's inventory identifier corresponds to the partially legible marking on a corroded equipment tag recovered from Waterworks Chamber L-02. The register records the lamp as unreturned following its assignment.
  informationType: 2
  isSceneExit: 0
  destinationScene: Diner_Investigation
  destinationSpawnID: 
  requiredInformationID: chamber_equipment_tag_marking
  unavailableMessage: The equipment registers cover many items. A marking or inventory number would narrow the search.
  department: Grayford Sheriff's Department
  documentTitle: Equipment Assignment Register
  reference: GSD-EAR-91-10
  documentDate: October 31, 1991
  documentBody: 'Equipment Assignment Entry



    Item: Portable Inspection Lamp

    Inventory ID: GSD-2714

    Assigned Officer: Deputy Michael Dwyer

    Date Issued: October 12, 1991



    Return Status: Not Recorded



    Administrative Remarks:

    Equipment listed as outstanding during the

    October inventory reconciliation.



    No transfer or disposal authorization is

    attached to this entry.



    Disposition: Pending verification.'
  evidenceID: dwyer_equipment_assignment_register
  evidenceTitle: Dwyer's Equipment Assignment
  journalNote: Inspection lamp GSD-2714 was assigned to Dwyer in October 1991 and was not recorded as returned. The chamber tag may bear the same number.
  evidenceSource: Grayford Sheriff's Department
